12. Configure ECS Service Auto Scaling

Go to:

ECS → Cluster → Service → Update

Enable:

Service auto scaling

Configure:

Plain Text
Minimum tasks: 1
Maximum tasks: 4
 

Target tracking policy:

Plain Text
Policy name:
httpd-cpu-autoscaling
 
Metric:
ECSServiceAverageCPUUtilization
 
Target:
50%
 
Scale-out cooldown:
300 seconds
 
Scale-in cooldown:
300 seconds

Save the configuration.
*************************************************************************************
13. Understand Auto Scaling

Your final normal configuration is:

Plain Text
Minimum = 1
Maximum = 4
CPU target = 50%
 

Conceptually:

Plain Text
CPU rises above target
↓
ECS Service Auto Scaling
↓
Desired task count increases
↓
New Fargate task starts
↓
Task registers with Target Group
↓
ALB sends traffic to healthy task

When demand decreases:

Plain Text
CPU decreases
↓
Auto Scaling evaluates utilization
↓
Desired task count decreases
↓
Extra Fargate tasks are stopped
 

During our test, we successfully observed scale-in from 3 tasks to 1 task.

Important: ECS Auto Scaling vs EC2 Auto Scaling

You asked why you couldn't see an Auto Scaling Group name.

That's because your application uses:

AWS Fargate

You configured:

ECS Service Auto Scaling

not:

EC2 Auto Scaling Group

So you should not expect an EC2 Auto Scaling Group for this architecture.
