14. ECS Exec Experiment

We also experimented with ECS Exec.

Initially you received:

Plain Text
InvalidParameterException:
valid taskRoleArn is not being used

We therefore created/used a Task IAM role and added the ECS Exec Systems Manager messaging permissions:

Plain Text
ssmmessages:CreateControlChannel
ssmmessages:CreateDataChannel
ssmmessages:OpenControlChannel
ssmmessages:OpenDataChannel

AWS documents these permissions for the ECS task role used with ECS Exec. ECS Exec Debugging Reference

We created a newer task definition revision with the task role and enabled ECS Exec:

Shell
aws ecs update-service \
--cluster harish-httpd-cluster \
--service httpd-alb-service \
--enable-execute-command \
--force-new-deployment \
--region ap-southeast-2

We verified:

Plain Text
enableExecuteCommand = true

And:

Plain Text
ExecuteCommandAgent
lastStatus: RUNNING

However, execute-command still returned:

Plain Text
TargetNotConnectedException

We stopped troubleshooting there, since ECS Exec wasn't necessary to complete the main ALB/Auto Scaling lab. AWS identifies TargetNotConnectedException as an ECS Exec troubleshooting scenario. Troubleshoot ECS Exec on Fargate errors

What you have learned from this lab

You can now explain these concepts in an interview:

ECS

Runs and manages containers.

Task Definition

Blueprint that tells ECS things such as:

Plain Text
Which image?
Which CPU/memory?
Which port?
Which IAM roles?
ECS Task

An actual running instance of the task definition.

ECS Service

Keeps the required number of tasks running.

Fargate

Runs containers without you managing EC2 worker servers.

Target Group

Tracks the backend targets that the ALB can send requests to.

For Fargate with awsvpc, we used:

Plain Text
Target type = IP
Application Load Balancer

Receives incoming HTTP traffic and distributes it to healthy ECS tasks.

Health Check

The ALB checks:

Plain Text
HTTP : 80
/

and only routes normal traffic to healthy targets.

Service Auto Scaling

Automatically changes the number of ECS tasks according to metrics such as CPU utilization.

